      "message": "I would expand a bit more here and specifically mention\n- the word \"shared\" makes it sound like anyone could know/derive the key... maybe point out that only the other party and ourselves knows it.. in particular I would point out that even if there were an active eavesdropper (\"Eve\") they don\u0027t have enough information to derive it. This would really help explain the awesomeness of key agreement!\n- what we\u0027re deriving could be used with e.g. AES encryption.. maybe even include a line such as `SecretKeySpec sessionEncryptionKey \u003d new SecretKeySpec(derivedKey, \"AES\")` at the end to drive home the point?\n- talk about info and salt parameters? I would perhaps just mention that this is usually prescribed by a higher level protocol but maybe it would be nice to explain what they are and how they are different from each other?\n\nMaybe it\u0027ll get too wordy/detailed with mentioning all this though. Thoughts?",
